.TH mmbc 1 "FUZIX System Utilities" "FUZIX"
.SH NAME
mmbc \- translate MMBasic to C
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mmbc
.I prog.bas
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mmbc
reads an MMBasic program and writes
.IR prog.c ,
which
.BR cc (1)
then compiles.  The three steps are:
.nf

# mmbc prog.bas          -> prog.c
# cc prog.c              -> prog.bc
# ./prog.bc              runs it

.fi
and
.B cc prog.bas
does all three at once.
.PP
This is a translator, not an interpreter.  The BASIC becomes C, the C
becomes a program, and what runs is the program \- which is why a
program written for the PicoMite runs faster here than on the machine it
was written for.
.SH WHAT IT COVERS
The graphics, sound, pin, file, string and maths words of MMBasic, and
the WEB family for networking.  What is implemented, and where it
deliberately diverges from the reference, is in the PC3 manual.
.SH ERRORS
An unknown keyword or an unsupported option is reported and stops the
translation.  It is not quietly dropped: a program that translates has
had every statement in it understood.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# mmbc hello.bas
# cc hello.c
# ./hello.bc
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cc (1),
.BR bcrun (1),
.BR mmedit (1)
